cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Validated NACA 0012 aerodynamics and one-way wind-turbine fluid-structure
  interaction in ANSYS Fluent and Mechanical
message: If you refer to this work, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jad
    family-names: El Badaoui
    affiliation: University of Bristol
abstract: >-
  Two linked simulation studies. A two-dimensional steady RANS solution over a
  NACA 0012 section at 10 degrees incidence and a chord Reynolds number of 6e6,
  carried from hand calculation and the governing equations through mesh design and
  the finite-volume method to formal numerical verification and validation against
  NASA experimental surface-pressure data. That aerofoil work then feeds a one-way
  coupled fluid-structure interaction study of a three-bladed horizontal-axis wind
  turbine, in which a rotating-frame CFD solution on a 120-degree periodic sector
  produces the aerodynamic pressure field that loads an orthotropic composite shell
  model. Includes a dependency-free pre-analysis calculator that reproduces every
  quoted hand calculation, and an explicit account of what is verified, what is
  validated, and what is neither.
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - ANSYS Fluent
  - finite volume method
  - RANS turbulence modelling
  - fluid-structure interaction
  - verification and validation
  - grid convergence
  - wind turbine
  - aerodynamics
  - aerospace engineering
